#nexus

[The TCS network of the ITS haplotypes of Syntrichia sarconeurum and S. lithophila, as in Figure 2b of
 Saluga, Ochyra & Ronikier (2022, J. Biogeogr. 49:1991-2004): what the TCS method of PopART computes on the
 deposited alignment ALIGNMENT_ITS_Haplotype_Network_116_SEQ (Dryad, doi:10.5061/dryad.h18931zp3) when the
 columns with a gap or missing data are masked. The unlabeled vertex that joins R05, R13 and R15 by one step
 each is as PopART draws it; it has no sequence, as R13 and R15 differ at four sites. PAT-05 has the
 sequence of R17 on the unmasked columns and is part of R17 in the published figure. In the published
 figure the edges of 16 and 14 mutations are drawn with 12 and 10 hatch marks.
 Excess and shortfall are measured against the sequence differences on the 40 variable unmasked columns.]

